data/*
# Driver scripts are the runbook in runnable form, and `data/*` above swallowed
# them: every data/*.sh in this repo's history is untracked, including the whole
# earlier campaign set. These three are whitelisted because they carry the
# 2026-10-01 corrective work (NOTES.md *Traps*): a pinned interpreter, a guard
# whose exit status is not piped away, and a launch gate read from the resolved
# config rather than inferred from a load-dependent epoch time. The older
# data/*.sh remain untracked -- adopting them is a separate call.
!data/m5_sweeps.sh
!data/clear_run.sh
!data/move_ckpts_to_data.sh
# every novel-view sweep publishes (eval_log.json + rollout videos), so a new
# sweep needs no .gitignore edit; the multi-GB zarrs/checkpoints stay out
!data/eval_*/
!data/eval_*/**
# relational-probe (step 1a) outputs: one small JSON per checkpoint, and the JSON *is* the
# measurement artifact -- every number is re-derivable from it without re-running.
!data/probe_relpose_*/
!data/probe_relpose_*/**
# the single-view z_g decode (same probe, --stability-ranges "1,1"). PROGRESS.md's Stage 2
# of *the second failure mode* reads latent_grid["1,1"].zg_abs_pose straight out of these,
# and until 2026-09-25 NONE of them were tracked -- the Artifacts table in NOTES.md claimed
# otherwise, so a committed headline result rested on box-only files.
!data/probe_zg_*/
!data/probe_zg_*/**
# collapse screens (screen_collapse.py): one small JSON per checkpoint, ditto.
!data/screen_collapse/
!data/screen_collapse/**
# conditioning screens (screen_conditioning.py): ditto.
!data/screen_conditioning/
!data/screen_conditioning/**
# latent-series analysis (analyze_latent_series.py): one JSON + one markdown per
# run (<500 KB total). The 328 MB of latent_snapshots/epoch_*.npz stay on the
# training box under /data and are never committed; the digest is the durable
# record of the raw-latent numbers (every one re-derivable from it). The driver
# runs on the training box only -- data/*.sh are untracked by default, see the
# comment at the top.
!data/analysis_*/
!data/analysis_*/**
!data/clear_analysis.sh
# 2026-10-07 follow-ups on the clear run: the held-out sweep (azimuth_offgrid
# preset) and the latent-distribution compute. Same rationale as clear_analysis.
!data/clear_heldout_eval.sh
!data/clear_latent_viz.sh
# 2026-10-08: the z_v-supervision run -- the clear run's recipe with the aux
# target's frame swapped camera -> base. The run driver's header carries the
# PRE-REGISTRATION (the read-out bands for the m4clear-vs-m4base A/B), which is
# only meaningful if it travels with the code; same rationale as the
# clear-run drivers above.
!data/m4base_run.sh
!data/m4base_eval.sh
!data/m4base_analysis.sh
# 2026-10-09: the z_g pose-set supervision run (PLAN candidate 2) -- m4base's
# recipe with the fused latent supervised on the live views' pooled camera-pose
# set. The run driver's header carries the PRE-REGISTRATION (the two-outcome
# latent diagnostic and the weight formula); same rationale as the m4base
# drivers above.
!data/zgpose_run.sh
!data/zgpose_eval.sh
!data/zgpose_analysis.sh
# 2026-10-12: the combined-supervision run (zvzg) -- m4base's per-view
# base-frame action head on z_v AND zgpose's pooled camera-pose set on z_g,
# both live at once. The run driver's header carries the PRE-REGISTRATION
# (both terms' bands, the tension readout); same rationale as the
# m4base/zgpose drivers above.
!data/zvzg_run.sh
!data/zvzg_eval.sh
!data/zvzg_analysis.sh
# 2026-10-15: the probabilistic-fusion runs (prob, cells B/C/D) -- per-view
# Gaussian (mu, logvar) heads + a selectable fusion (MHA-over-mu / PoE /
# mean-of-mu) on the m4base recipe; cell A is the committed m4base run. The
# run driver's header carries the PRE-REGISTRATION (bands vs A, the mechanism
# gates, the claimed-and-CPU-pinned RNG lockstep); same rationale as the
# m4base/zgpose/zvzg drivers above.
!data/prob_run.sh
!data/prob_eval.sh
# 2026-10-16: the prob round's INSTRUMENT battery (digest + viz coords + screens
# + the relpose grid + the deferred variance-quality read). Same rationale as
# the *_analysis.sh drivers above; the variance script's header carries the
# thresholds the run driver deferred to it.
!data/prob_analysis.sh
# 2026-10-16: the z-supervision round (PLAN_Z) -- the m4base recipe plus
# cross-view shared-semantics alignment on z_v (L_align, a shared projection
# head) and cross-view action consistency on z_g (L_cons, two independent view
# draws through the UNet). The run driver's header carries the PRE-REGISTRATION
# (bands vs m4base, the mechanism gates, the claimed-and-CPU-pinned RNG
# contract, the lambda calibration rule); same rationale as the drivers above.
!data/z_run.sh
!data/z_eval.sh
!data/z_analysis.sh
# 2026-10-28: the encoder ladder's B baseline -- the M3 encoder on the clear
# run's K=11 recipe with the corrected EE-history protocol. B0/B1 differ by one
# flag (`task.dataset.eef_hist_window`); the run driver's header carries the
# PRE-REGISTRATION (the banded B1-B0 comparison) and the history-protocol
# rationale. Same tracking rule as the drivers above.
!data/enc_b_run.sh
!data/enc_b_eval.sh
# 2026-10-28: the encoder ladder's S stage -- pure-RGB ResNet18 layer3 spatial
# tokens read by one shared query, then the original cross-view fusion. The run
# driver's header carries the PRE-REGISTRATION (the banded S-B1 comparison,
# the non-pairing RNG note, the mechanism-live gates). Same tracking rule.
!data/enc_s_run.sh
!data/enc_s_eval.sh
# 2026-10-29: the encoder ladder's R stage -- S plus feature-level ray
# encoding on the attention key. The run driver's header carries the
# PRE-REGISTRATION (R vs S on the ring, the non-pairing RNG note, the
# mechanism-live gates and the `use_ray_encoding=False` diagnostic). Same
# tracking rule.
!data/enc_r_run.sh
!data/enc_r_eval.sh
# 2026-10-29: the encoder ladder's RH/RHG stages -- R plus the base-frame
# trajectory-conditioned shared query (RH), then the point-to-ray attention
# bias on 4/8 heads (RHG). The run drivers' headers carry the PRE-REGISTRATION
# (RH vs R, RHG vs RH, the banded means and the mechanism-live gates); the
# RHG driver also calibrates and LOCKS sigma. The calibration JSON is the
# measurement artifact that fixes every later RHG cell's sigma, so it is
# tracked; data/enc_rhg_calib.env is a local run artifact, not whitelisted.
!data/enc_rh_run.sh
!data/enc_rh_eval.sh
!data/enc_rhg_run.sh
!data/enc_rhg_eval.sh
!data/enc_rhg_calib_square.json
# 2026-10-29: stage LQ -- LVSM RGB+Pluecker 8x8 patchify + EEF-history query
# tokens, one bidirectional transformer, only the query positions read out.
# The run driver's header carries the pre-registration (LQ vs B1/R/RH with
# the crop 76->72 confound, the two control flags) and the S=895 memory note.
!data/enc_lq_run.sh
!data/enc_lq_eval.sh
# z-supervision runs (za zalign / zb zcons / zc zboth): logs only, never the
# 4.6 GB checkpoints (same rule as the blocks below). The run driver's first
# shell writes data/z_calib_env.sh, the shared (W_ALIGN, W_CONS) -- a local
# run artifact, deliberately NOT whitelisted.
!data/outputs/run_*_za_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_za_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_za_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
!data/outputs/run_*_zb_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_zb_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_zb_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
!data/outputs/run_*_zc_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_zc_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_zc_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# ring montages only -- data/multiview/ also holds the multi-GB zarrs
!data/multiview/
data/multiview/*
!data/multiview/*.png
!data/outputs/
data/outputs/*
# Encoder ladder B0/B1/S: exceptions must come AFTER `data/outputs/*`; an
# earlier block is re-ignored by that rule. Logs only; the 4.6 GB checkpoints
# stay out.
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_b0_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_square_enc_b0_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_b0_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_b1_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_square_enc_b1_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_b1_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_s_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_square_enc_s_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_s_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_r_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_square_enc_r_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_r_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_rh_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_square_enc_rh_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_rh_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_rhg_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_square_enc_rhg_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_rhg_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_lq_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_square_enc_lq_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_square_enc_lq_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
!data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# M3 runs: the per-batch train/val/rollout curves, same rationale as M1's above.
# The 4.6 GB checkpoints stay out; only logs.json.txt (~9 MB/run) is published.
!data/outputs/run_*_m3*_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_m3*_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_m3*_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# ... and a seed-mate of an M3 cell, which the `_s42`-only pattern above silently drops --
# the same trap the L1 whitelist further down records. The `[1,5]` second seed exists
# precisely to measure the spread across two seeds of ONE config, so its training record
# is the run.
!data/outputs/run_*_m3*_s43_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_m3*_s43_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_m3*_s43_200ep/logs.json.txt
# M4 runs: same rationale. logs.json.txt carries the aux_loss curve, which is the
# primary evidence that the aux mechanism is learnable (see the M4 section of PROGRESS.md).
!data/outputs/run_*_m4*_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_m4*_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_m4*_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# z_g pose-set run: logs only, never the 4.6 GB checkpoints (same rule as the
# m4 runs above). A future seed-mate needs its own line -- the `_s42`-only trap
# the M3 and L1 blocks record.
!data/outputs/run_*_zgpose_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_zgpose_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_zgpose_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# combined-supervision run (zvzg): logs only, never the 4.6 GB checkpoints
# (same rule as the blocks above). A future seed-mate needs its own line --
# the `_s42`-only trap the M3 and L1 blocks record.
!data/outputs/run_*_zvzg_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_zvzg_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_zvzg_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# prob runs (cells B/C/D): logs only, never the 4.6 GB checkpoints (same rule
# as the blocks above). A future seed-mate needs its own line -- the `_s42`-only
# trap the M3 and L1 blocks record.
!data/outputs/run_*_prob_*_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_prob_*_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_prob_*_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# M1 re-train (2026-09-25): recovers the single-view baseline weights that were deleted
# 2026-09-19, so its ENCODER can be collapse-screened -- the question is whether the
# original baseline was itself collapsed. Same rule: logs only, never the checkpoints.
!data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_*200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_*200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_*200ep/logs.json.txt
# L1 (randview) runs: the s43 seed-mate of L1 square was missed by the original whitelist,
# so one committed number's only training record was absent from git. L1's seed-robustness
# claim (collapse screens agree to 26% across s42/s43) rests on that run.
!data/outputs/run_*_randview_s*_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_randview_s*_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_randview_s*_200ep/logs.json.txt
